I am offering the use of an agent I have created that automatically
generates, in your name, a "last-word" post on whatever threads you assign
it.  Once my agent is installed, merely send the command

  ::lastword thread foo

where "foo" is either a message ID or a search expression.  Thereafter,
whenever a message goes out to the list that continues that thread, the
agent automatically quotes a section of that message (using heuristics that
clear out signatures, Reply-To headers, and the like), generates a response
by running the entire previous text of that thread through "Disassociated
Press" and a "Word Perfect" spell checker (to generate _truly_
incomprehensible prose... "Metzger" transforms to "meshuga" and so forth),
appends your .signature to the whole thing, and sends it out to the list. 
The length of the new text generated is determined by a formula

        L(n+1) = L(n)^2 / L(n-1)

where L(n) is the length of message n of the thread.  This formula
continues the current trend in the size of messages in that particular
thread.

The "lastword" command is compatible with the "exclude" command, in that
"lastword" can reply to threads you have "excluded", permitting you to
participate in debates without ever knowing you are doing so.

"lastword" works with users as well; the command

  ::lastword user bar

causes the agent to reply automatically to any post by a particular user. 
Again, this is compatible with "exclude" -- your opponent need never know
that you are ignoring him or her completely, while it appears that you are
dogging his heels indefatigably.

Finally, this agent can accept a lexicon file of additional words and
phrases you want it to mix in with previous text from the thread -- giving
it your distinctive voice and style, or the voice and style you aspire to. 
Provide your agent with the "Penguin Dictionary of Economics" or a
philosophical encyclopedia, for example, and you can dazzle opponents with
your erudition on that subject without ever cracking a book.  Feed it "The
Way Things Ought To Be," and you can adopt the persona of Rush Limbaugh. 
And so forth.

Beta testing of the agent is now complete.  I have been asked by my beta
testers not to reveal their identities, but eleven list members have been
using my agent for the past month.  In fact, only one participant in the
"cheating the post office" thread was a real person (I am honor-bound not
to reveal who).

Contact me by private e-mail if you wish to secure the use of this
wonderful new product of the field of A.D. (Artificial Disputatiousness).

